---
import { siteConfig } from "../siteConfig";
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "@utils/withBase";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <main
    class="grow pt-28 lg:pt-32 pb-12 px-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto w-full prose dark:prose-invert prose-a:text-primary"
  >
    <a class="text-sm no-underline hover:underline" href={withBase("/projects")}
      >Projects</a
    >
    <h1 class="font-heading tracking-tighter">About JOSH</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      {siteConfig.name} (JOSH) is a catalogue of open source hardware developed
      by teams at Janelia Research Campus.
    </p>

    <h2>What you will find here</h2>
    <p>
      Each project has a page describing the hardware and linking to where its
      design files are hosted, which may be GitHub, Figshare or another site.
      Where a project has a Figshare record, the page also shows its authors,
      DOI and a ready-made citation, so the design can be cited when it is used.
    </p>
    <p>
      Projects are tagged so you can check what you need before you download
      anything:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>File types</strong> lists the formats in the download. Proprietary
        formats are marked "(proprietary)".
      </li>
      <li><strong>License</strong> says how the design may be used.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>CAD/EDA</strong> names the design tools the files were made with.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Hardware type</strong>, <strong>use case</strong> and
        <strong>development team</strong> help you find related designs.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Browse the <a href={withBase("/projects")}>card view</a> to filter and
      search, or use the <a href={withBase("/projects-table")}>table view</a> to
      scan every project in one list.
    </p>

    <h2>Add your hardware</h2>
    <p>
      We welcome contributions from current and former Janelians. To add a
      project, contact <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}
        >{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a
      >.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
